  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 6330, the IRS must provide notice and an opportunity for a Collection Due Process (CDP) hearing before levying a taxpayer''s wages, bank accounts, or other property. This pre-levy hearing right is a statutory protection for taxpayers.
Wrong (A): Refund offsets do not require a CDP hearing; the IRS may offset refunds against outstanding liabilities without prior notice.
Wrong (B): Filing a federal tax lien requires post-filing notice within 5 business days under Section 6320, but not a pre-filing hearing.
