-- Q2457: Business Law: Contracts [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under UCC Section 2-201 and common law, the MYLEGS mnemonic represents: Marriage (promises in consideration of marriage), Year (contracts not performable within one year), Land (interests in real property), Executor (executor''s personal promise to pay estate debts), Goods (sale of goods $500 or more), and Suretyship (promises to answer for another''s debt).
Wrong (A): "Money" and "Estates" are not accurate Statute of Frauds categories; the correct terms are Marriage and Executor promises.
Wrong (B): "Mortgages," "Licenses," and "General partnerships" are not among the six Statute of Frauds categories.
Wrong (C): "Minors," "Gifts," and "Services" are not Statute of Frauds categories; the mnemonic does not address capacity or gift law.$EXPL$
