  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Restatement (Second) of Contracts Section 302, an intended third-party beneficiary may enforce the contract once the beneficiary''s rights vest. Vesting occurs when the beneficiary learns of and assents to the contract, materially changes position in reliance, or brings suit.
Wrong (B): No court order is required for vesting; it occurs by the beneficiary''s own actions such as reliance or assent.
Wrong (C): An intended beneficiary has enforceable rights even though not a party to the contract, unlike an incidental beneficiary.
Wrong (D): An intended beneficiary need not provide consideration; the beneficiary''s rights arise from the contract between the original parties.$EXPL$
