  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under UCC Section 2-601, the perfect tender rule permits a buyer to reject goods if the goods or their delivery fail to conform to the contract in any respect. The buyer may reject the whole, accept the whole, or accept any commercial units and reject the rest.
Wrong (B): The perfect tender rule does not require a materiality threshold or a 10% value reduction; any nonconformity suffices for rejection.
