  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under UCC Section 2-205, a firm offer by a merchant in a signed writing that assures the offer will be held open is irrevocable for the stated period (up to 3 months) without consideration. This is an exception to the common law rule requiring consideration for option contracts.
Wrong (A): A deposit is not required; UCC Section 2-205 expressly eliminates the consideration requirement for merchant firm offers in signed writings.
Wrong (B): While common law requires consideration for irrevocable offers, UCC Section 2-205 provides a specific exception for merchants.
