  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under the common law pre-existing duty rule in Restatement (Second) of Contracts Section 73, a contract modification requires new consideration from both parties to be enforceable. Performing an existing obligation does not constitute valid consideration for a new promise.
Wrong (B): Under common law, modifications are not always valid without consideration; unlike UCC Section 2-209, the pre-existing duty rule applies to service contracts.
