  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 8.01, the duty of loyalty requires an agent to disclose all material information, avoid self-dealing, and not compete with the principal. Mitchell must disclose the developer''s above-market offer and refrain from purchasing the property for personal profit.
Wrong (B): An agent is not required to work exclusively for one principal; dual agency is permitted with proper disclosure and consent.
